      "explanation": "C is correct. If principal = P, amount = 2P. SI = 2P-P = P. Rate = SI×100/(P×T) = P×100/(P×8) = 100/8 = 12.5%. Short trick: If a sum doubles in T years at SI, rate = 100/T. Here T=8, rate = 100/8 = 12.5%. Trap: 10% = 100/10 (correct for T=10, not T=8); 12% = wrong rounding.",
      "staleness_risk": 0,
      "answer_source": "generated"
