      "correct_letter": "C",
      "difficulty": "HARD",
      "explanation": "C is correct. Let each sum = P. SI₁ = P×5×4/100 = 20P/100. SI₂ = P×6×4/100 = 24P/100. Difference = 24P/100 - 20P/100 = 4P/100 = 200. P = 200×100/4 = Rs. 5,000. Verify: SI at 5% = 5000×5×4/100=1000; SI at 6%=5000×6×4/100=1200. Difference=200 ✓. Trap: 4,000: diff=4000×4×4/4×100=160≠200; 6,000: diff=6000×4/100=240≠200.",
